# Panic-by-default: `expect(msg)` on a `None` value traps (reference §15.2).
# NOTE: the test asserts ONLY a bug-agnostic substring (`` `None` value ``),
# NOT the full message. Threading the user-supplied `expect` message through to
# the panic text is a SEPARATE filed TODO — until it lands, `expect` reuses the
# generic `unwrap()` message, so pinning the full text here would cement the
# dropped-message bug as canonical output. Once the threading lands, this fixture
# should assert the user message ("need a value") instead.
void main():
    Option[int] o = None
    print(o.expect("need a value"))
